> repair instead of enchanting.  But you get better AC with those
> helms/boots by enchanting them than by fixing them. 

Something I realized only recently is that manual armor-proofing is 
mostly pointless.  When you have ?EA, it is more effective to increase 
the enchantment of your existing armor, rather than protect them against 
a possible future danger that may never come, and will at worse take away 
1-2 points of AC per item.  And once all your armor is at +4/+5, you have 
more than enough AC to ascend with, and can afford to let them rust.  If 
you have extra ?EA, you might as well use them, but it won't change the 
eventual outcome of your game.

Of course, if you find a c?DA, you should certainly confuse yourself and 
use it.  This is especially true early on -- but unfortunately you 
probably won't find it and a good confusion source early on.

